{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794547490475,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d35d9c250010bf4nzthzrIEeY","sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","messageID":"msg_1d35d7db200103cVEYthpRcDDp","type":"tool","id":"call_6c1eb0a93f064c0d8800d8f4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md","limit":120},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md, lines 1-120\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 13: attribution-and-install-reach\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that return injected context from four session readers, decide brief delivery from it and from the Codex approval, fix the scorer's offer, safety and start counts, restore a turn to HEAD in a tested module, refuse an unapproved Codex arm, leave a CLAUDE.md pointer on embed, add a delivery leg to /doctor:setup and keep the command fields the OpenCode plugin drops.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"attribution and install reach tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 13: attribution-and-install-reach\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a live model session, an arena or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `VALL` is `npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n31: - `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers`. `SRT` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers`. `VSR` is `node --test $SRT/*.test.mjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `SRD` is `node .skilled/hooks/shared/session-reader-declarations.mjs`, and `SRD --check` must print a line containing `current`. `SRR` is `$SR/README.md`.\n32: - `OF` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` and `OT` its test `$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`. `VO` is `npx vitest run tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n33: - `S` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `T` its test `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. `VT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `R` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`. `WR` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/worktree-restore.mjs` (new) and `WRT` its test `$ADV/tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts` (new). `VWR` is `npx vitest run tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n35: - `CAP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`. `CORPUS` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`.\n36: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `EMB` is `$DS/agents-md-embed.cjs` and `EMBT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs`. `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs` and `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`. `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs`. `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n37: - `DAM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md`. `DAE` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`. `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DSP` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`. `DSM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`. `IG` is `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`.\n38: - `P7` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch`. `POST` is `$P7/runs-post-final.jsonl`, `PRE` is `$P7/runs-pre-final.jsonl` and `G2` is `$P7/runs-g2.jsonl`. These three logs are read-only. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n39: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print a `correct` of at least 24 over 44 and exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n40: - `EVAL` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which must print numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5.\n41: - `RV` is `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh`, which must exit 0. `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0.\n42: - `BRIEF` is the head `Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.82/0.12 pass.`, used as fixture text.\n43: - `PLG` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, the OpenCode plugin. It is authored in place, and `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js` is a link to it. `PLT` is `$ADV/tests/system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts` and `VPL` is `npx vitest run tests/system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `NPL` is `node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `PLR` is `.opencode/plugins/README.md`. `PROBE` is `node $SP/planning/probe-opencode-brief.mjs`, which loads `PLG` with its CLI call stubbed by the real advisor answer for `/create:readme for the utils folder` and prints the brief head.\n44: \n45: Rules for every task:\n46: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it.\n47: - No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout` in `CORPUS`. Scripts print row ids only.\n48: - No worker starts a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its stores under a temporary folder. Reading a store under the home folder is allowed only in T002, T033 and T034, and only through the shared readers or `CK`.\n49: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T037 checks it.\n50: - Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, any file under `.skilled/commands/create/`, any `package.json` or any routing input. Add no dependency.\n51: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n52: - When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n53: \n54: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n55: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`), T002 (`$SP/summary-*-before.json`, `$SP/delivery-before.txt`). Read-only for the repository.\n56: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phase 011 is committed and that phase 012's diff touches none of the files named below.\n57: - Wave 1: T003 (`$SR/claude.mjs`, `$SRT/claude.test.mjs`), T004 (`$SR/pi.mjs`, `$SRT/pi.test.mjs`), T005 (`$SR/devin.mjs`, `$SRT/devin.test.mjs`), T006 (`$SR/dsh.mjs`, `$SRT/dsh.test.mjs`), T007 (`OF`, `OT`), T008 (`S`, `T`), T009 (`EMB`, `EMBT`), T010 (`CHK`, `CHKT`), T011 (`WR`, `WRT`), T012 (`DSY`).\n58: - Wave 2: T013 (`$SR/index.mjs`, `$SRT/injected-text.test.mjs`), T014 (`OF`, `OT`), T015 (`S`, `T`), T016 (`DSP`), T017 (`DSM`), T018 (`DAM`, `DAE`), T019 (`IG`).\n59: - Wave 3: T020 (`$SR/*.d.mts`, `$SR/*.d.mts.map`), T021 (`OF`, `OT`), T022 (`S`, `T`), T023 (`R`).\n60: - Wave 4: T024 (`R`), T025 (`S`, `T`), T026 (`SRR`).\n61: - Wave 5: T027 (`R`), T028 (`S`, `T`).\n62: - Wave 6: T029 (`R`), T030 (`S`, `T`), T031 (`CAP`).\n63: - Wave 7: T032 (`RA`).\n64: - Gate: wave 7b starts only after phase 012 is committed, because only phase 012's renderer prints `needsMode`.\n65: - Wave 7b: T039 (`PLG`, `PLT`), T040 (`PLR`).\n66: - Wave 8, one at a time: T033 (`$SP/runs-post-attributed.jsonl`), T034 (`$SP/summary-*-after.json`), T035 (`$SP/delivery-leg.txt`).\n67: - Verification, one at a time: T036, T037, T038.\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n73: ## Phase 1: Setup\n74: \n75: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `VSR`, `SRD --check`, `DALL`, `RV`, `SRM`, `VO`, `VT` and `git rev-parse --short HEAD`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL`, `VO` and `VT` report 0 failed, `VSR` and `DALL` report `fail 0`, `SRD --check` prints `current`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 12. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\n76: - [x] T002 Record the three arms and the delivery state (`$SP/summary-post-before.json`, `$SP/summary-pre-before.json`, `$SP/summary-g2-before.json`, `$SP/delivery-before.txt`). Run `node $S --summary $POST --json > $SP/summary-post-before.json`, the same for `PRE` and `G2` into their files, then `jq -c '{r:.runtime,b:.briefDelivered}' $POST | sort | uniq -c > $SP/delivery-before.txt`, and append to that file the output of `for d in $(jq -r '.locator.projectDir' $POST | sort -u); do test -d \"$d\" && echo \"present $d\" || echo \"missing $d\"; done` and of `node $CK --root \"$(jq -r 'select(.runtime==\"codex\") | .locator.projectDir' $POST | head -1)\" | head -1`. Verify: `jq -r 'keys | join(\",\")' $SP/summary-post-before.json` lists the six runtimes, `rg -c '\"b\":\"unknown\"' $SP/delivery-before.txt` prints 5, `rg -c '^present ' $SP/delivery-before.txt` prints 6 and the last line starts with `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved`. When an arena is missing, record it and go on: T033 will mark Codex `[B]`.\n77: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n82: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n83: \n84: ### Wave 1\n85: - [ ] T003 [P] Return Claude's injected hook context (`$SR/claude.mjs`, `$SRT/claude.test.mjs`). Add a function `injectedFromEntries(entries)` that, for every entry with `type` `attachment` and `attachment.type` `hook_additional_context`, takes its `attachment.content` as text (a string as is, an array by joining each string item and each item's `text` with `\\n`) and returns `[{ source: 'hook_additional_context', text }]` for each non-empty text, in file order. In `loadClaudeSession`, add `injected: injectedFromEntries(entries)` to the ok result after `records`. Change nothing else. In the test file add one case: a Claude fixture with one extra line `{ type: 'attachment', attachment: { type: 'hook_additional_context', hookEvent: 'UserPromptSubmit', content: [BRIEF] } }` loads with `injected` equal to `[{ source: 'hook_additional_context', text: BRIEF }]` and the same `records` length as the fixture without it. Verify: `node --test $SRT/claude.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n86: - [ ] T004 [P] Return Pi's custom messages (`$SR/pi.mjs`, `$SRT/pi.test.mjs`). Add `injectedFromLines(lines)`: for each line with `type` `custom_message`, `text` is `contentText(line.content)`, and it returns `[{ source: line.customType ?? 'custom_message', text }]` for each non-empty text. Add `injected: injectedFromLines(entries)` to the live result and `injected: injectedFromLines(lines)` to the disk result, after `records`. In the test file add one case: a disk fixture with an appended `{ type: 'custom_message', customType: 'session-start-context', id: 'pi-context', content: BRIEF }` loads through `loadPiSession` with `injected` `[{ source: 'session-start-context', text: BRIEF }]` and no record whose id is `pi-context`. Verify: `node --test $SRT/pi.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n87: - [ ] T005 [P] Return Devin's system and unflagged user nodes (`$SR/devin.mjs`, `$SRT/devin.test.mjs`). Add `injectedFromChain(chain)`: for each node whose parsed `chat_message` has `role` `system`, or `role` `user` with `metadata.is_user_input` neither `true` nor `1`, and a non-empty string `content`, return `{ source: <role, or 'unflagged-user' for the user case>, text: content }`. Change `recordsFromDatabase` to return `null` as today when the chain is missing and otherwise `{ records: recordsFromChain(chain), injected: injectedFromChain(chain) }` (an empty session returns `{ records: [], injected: [] }`), and update the one caller in `loadDevinSession` to read `.records` and add `injected` after `records`. In `loadTranscript`, add `injected` built from steps whose `source` is neither `user` nor `agent` and whose `message` is a non-empty string, `{ source: step.source, text: step.message }`. In the test file add one case: `devinSession({ root, projectDir, compacted: true })` loads with an `injected` entry whose `source` is `system` and whose text starts with `You are continuing work`, and the `records` roles match the existing compacted case. Verify: `node --test $SRT/devin.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n88: - [ ] T006 [P] Return DSH's injected notices (`$SR/dsh.mjs`, `$SRT/dsh.test.mjs`). Add `injectedFromEvents(events)`: for each event with `type` `user/message` whose `data.source?.kind` is not `user`, `text` is `contentText(data.content)`, and it returns `[{ source: data.source?.kind ?? 'unknown', text }]` for each non-empty text. Add `injected: injectedFromEvents(events)` to the ok result after `records`. In the test file add one case: a fixture with an appended `user/message` whose source kind is `repo-guards` and whose content is `[{ type: 'text', text: BRIEF }]` loads with `injected` `[{ source: 'repo-guards', text: BRIEF }]`. Verify: `node --test $SRT/dsh.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n89: - [ ] T007 [P] Ask the Codex approval check before reading Codex delivery (`OF`, `OT`). Import `fileURLToPath` from `node:url` and define `REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../../../../..')` and `CODEX_CHECK = join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs')`. Export `codexHookApproval({ projectDir, configPath } = {})`: return `'unknown'` when `projectDir` is not a non-empty string, else run `spawnSync('node', [CODEX_CHECK, '--root', projectDir, '--json', ...(configPath ? ['--config', configPath] : [])], { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 10_000 })`, parse stdout as JSON and map `code` `codex-hooks-approved` to `'approved'`, `codex-hooks-unapproved` to `'unapproved'`, `codex-advisor-hook-absent` to `'absent'`, `no-codex-hooks` to `'no-hooks'` and anything else, a spawn error or unparsable output to `'unknown'`. In `briefDelivered`, add an option `codexConfig` and a `codex` branch before the final return: when `codexHookApproval({ projectDir: locator?.projectDir, configPath: codexConfig })` is `'unapproved'` return `false`. Otherwise return `'unknown'` when `loadSession` is not a function or the load is not ok, `true` when `recordsHaveBrief(loaded.records)` and `'unknown'` otherwise. Add a comment saying an unapproved project hook never runs, so the brief cannot have arrived, while an approved one may store its context where no reader looks yet. In `OT`, add cases on a temporary root holding `.codex/hooks.json` with `{\"hooks\":{\"UserPromptSubmit\":[{\"hooks\":[{\"command\":\"node x/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js\"}]}]}}`: an empty config file gives `'unapproved'`, a config holding `[hooks.state.\"<realpath of root>/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:0:0\"]` then `trusted_hash = \"x\"` gives `'approved'`, a root with no `.codex` gives `'no-hooks'`, and `briefDelivered({ runtime: 'codex', locator: { projectDir: root }, codexConfig: <empty config> })` resolves to `false`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n90: - [ ] T008 [P] Count an expected offer on every scored row (`S`, `T`). In `addScored`, move the offered count out of the start-row block: when `result.offered` add 1 to `offered`, and also add 1 to a new `cappedOfferRows` when `result.capped`, else add 1 to `startedOfOffered` when `result.started`. Keep the `offerUnknown` count where it is for now. Add `cappedOfferRows: 0` to `newTally` and `cappedOfferRows` to `tallyBlock` after `offered`. In `writeSummary`, print `offered ${block.offered} (${block.cappedOfferRows} capped), started ${block.startedOfOffered} of ${block.offered - block.cappedOfferRows}` in place of the current offered clause. Add a comment saying an offer is a fact about the head the reader saw, so it counts whatever the row's policy and whether the turn hit its cap. In `T`, add one summary case: `SUMMARY_ROW` with `exit: 143` and `offeredCommand: '/create:agent'` plus `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-02` with `exit: 0` and the same offer give `offered: 2, cappedOfferRows: 1, startedOfOffered: 1`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed and `node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post | [.offered,.cappedOfferRows,.startedOfOffered])'` prints `{\"claude\":[3,0,1],\"codex\":[3,0,0],\"devin\":[3,0,1],\"dsh\":[3,0,2],\"opencode\":[3,2,0],\"pi\":[3,1,1]}`.\n91: - [ ] T009 [P] Leave an `@AGENTS.md` pointer where `embed` would remove or never write `CLAUDE.md` (`EMB`, `EMBT`). Add `const CLAUDE_POINTER_PATH = 'CLAUDE.md'` and, in the composer, build the pointer text as `` `@${manifest.root_file}\\n` ``. In the loop that pushes removed copies into `files` (the one after the mirror block), push `{ path: copy.path, action: 'replace', content: <pointer text>, before: copy.content }` when `copy.path` is `CLAUDE.md`, and keep `remove` for every other copy. Leave `removedCopies` unchanged, so the survival proof still checks the folded lines. Just before `composition.writes` is computed, when `files` already holds an entry whose action is `create`, `replace` or `remove`, and `CLAUDE.md` neither exists nor is a symlink under `root`, push `{ path: 'CLAUDE.md', action: 'create', content: <pointer text>, before: null }`. Change the `--remove-claude-md` usage line to `fold it and leave an @AGENTS.md pointer in its place (the default)`. Add a comment saying Claude Code reads only `CLAUDE.md`, so the pointer is its one route to the root document. In `EMBT`, change exactly two assertions, because they pin the removal this change replaces: line 638 becomes `assert.equal(readInside(dir, 'CLAUDE.md'), '@AGENTS.md\\n', 'the folded copy became a pointer')` and line 842 becomes `assert.equal(readInside(dir, 'CLAUDE.md'), '@AGENTS.md\\n')`. Add one case: an `adopted` tree with no `CLAUDE.md` whose apply writes the root document also creates `CLAUDE.md` reading `@AGENTS.md\\n`. Verify: `node --test $EMBT` reports `fail 0`, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 HEAD -- $EMBT | rg -c \"^-\\s+assert\"` prints 2 and `rg -n \"keepClaudeMd\" $EMB` still prints the parse line and the keep branch.\n92: - [ ] T010 [P] Report a missing Claude pointer in A10 (`CHK`, `CHKT`). In `copyVerdict`, before the `if (!exists)` block, return `{ state: INFO, kind: 'pointer missing', detail: 'Claude Code reads only CLAUDE.md, so without a one-line @' + manifest.root_file + ' pointer it never loads ' + manifest.root_file }` when `expected.path` is `CLAUDE.md`, the file neither exists nor is a symlink and `context.exists` is true. In `rowRuntimeCopies`, also push the `${expected.path}: ${verdict.kind} - ${verdict.detail}` line when the kind is `pointer missing`. Keep the row's state rule as it is, so INFO leaves A10 PASS. Rewrite the comment above `rowRuntimeCopies` to say Claude Code reaches the root document only through `CLAUDE.md`, so a missing pointer leaves Claude without it and a full copy double-loads and drifts. In `CHKT`, add one case: a `pure` fixture with no `CLAUDE.md` gives the `CLAUDE.md` entry `kind` `pointer missing` and `state` `INFO`, the A10 row `state` `PASS` and a line starting `CLAUDE.md: pointer missing`. Verify: `node --test $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `node $CHK | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` prints 1.\n93: - [ ] T011 [P] Create the turn restore module and its test (`WR`, `WRT`). `WR` exports `statusSnapshot(cwd)`, which runs `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain` in `cwd` and returns a `Map` from path to its two-letter code, with both sides of a rename as separate keys, and `restoreTurn({ cwd, before })`. `restoreTurn` takes `after = statusSnapshot(cwd)` and the changed paths, those in `after` whose code differs from `before` and that are not keys of `before`. For each, with any trailing `/` removed: when `git cat-file -e HEAD:<path>` exits 0 run `git checkout HEAD -- <path>`, else run `git rm -r -q --cached --ignore-unmatch -- <path>` and then `rmSync(resolve(cwd, path), { recursive: true, force: true })`, collecting a failure message for any non-zero exit or throw. It then takes `final = statusSnapshot(cwd)` and returns `{ restored, leftoverPaths, failures }`, where `leftoverPaths` is every path whose code in `final` differs from its code in `before`, in either direction and sorted, and `restored` is true only when both lists are empty. A path that is a key of `before` is never passed to a git command or `rmSync`. Add a comment saying a staged new file is in the index, so restoring from the index keeps it, and only HEAD is the state the turn started from. `WRT` builds a temporary repository with `git init` and one commit of `kept.txt`, using `-c user.name=fixture -c user.email=fixture@example.invalid` on the commit, and covers: a turn that writes and `git add`s `new.txt`, edits and `git add`s `kept.txt`, and writes `out/a.txt` restores to an empty porcelain status with `kept.txt` back to its committed text and `restored` true. An untracked `note.txt` present before the snapshot that the turn then `git add`s is left in place, with `restored` false and `leftoverPaths` `['note.txt']`. A turn that changes nothing returns `restored` true. Verify: `VWR` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n94: - [ ] T012 [P] Add the delivery leg to the setup workflow (`DSY`). Change `six` to `seven` in `purpose` and `action`. Add `hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"` and `codex_approval_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"` under `upstream_assets`. After the `Leg embedder` step, add one step: `\"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"` Verify: `rg -c \"seven\" $DSY` prints 2, `rg -c \"six\" $DSY` prints 0, `rg -c \"Leg delivery\" $DSY` prints 1 and `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-setup-orphan-line.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`.\n95: \n96: ### Wave 2\n97: - [ ] T013 [P] Pass injected context through `loadSession` (`$SR/index.mjs`, `$SRT/injected-text.test.mjs`). In `loadSession`, return `{ ok: true, source: loaded.source, records: loaded.records, ...(Array.isArray(loaded.injected) ? { injected: loaded.injected } : {}) }`. Leave `readSession` as it is. In the test file, add one case: the Pi fixture from the existing Pi case, loaded through `loadSession` from the index, carries `injected` with the `custom_message` text, and the same session through `readSession` returns no item whose id is `pi-context`. Verify: `VSR` reports `fail 0` and `node -e \"import('./.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs').then(async m => { const r = await m.loadSession({ runtime: 'codex', sessionId: 'x', transcriptPath: '/nonexistent/x.jsonl' }); console.log(Object.keys(r).join(',')) })\"` prints `ok,code`.\n98: - [ ] T014 [P] Decide Pi, Devin and DSH delivery from records and injected context (`OF`, `OT`). Add `injectedHasBrief(injected)`, true when any entry's `text` matches `BRIEF_PATTERN`. Change the `pi` branch to cover `pi`, `devin` and `dsh` and return `recordsHaveBrief(loaded.records) || injectedHasBrief(loaded.injected)`. In the `codex` branch, return `true` when either test holds. Update the function's doc comment to name the five runtimes and the reason OpenCode stays `unknown`: its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy. In `OT`, add cases with an injected `loadSession`: `devin` with `{ ok: true, records: [], injected: [{ source: 'system', text: BRIEF }] }` resolves `true`, `dsh` with empty `records` and `injected` resolves `false`, and `opencode` with a brief in its records resolves `'unknown'`. Keep the existing `devin` case without a reader, which must still resolve `'unknown'`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n99: - [ ] T015 [P] Rename `offerUnknown` to `offerFieldAbsent` and count it on every scored row (`S`, `T`). In `offerOf`, `scoreRun`, its doc comment, `newTally` and `tallyBlock`, rename the key. In `addScored`, remove the `else if (result.offerUnknown)` branch and add `if (result.offerFieldAbsent) tally.offerFieldAbsent += 1;` beside the other every-row counts. In `writeSummary`, print `offer field absent ${block.offerFieldAbsent}`. In `T`, rename the key in the case at line 724, which keeps its value 0. Verify: `rg -c \"offerUnknown|offer unknown\" $S $T` prints nothing, `VT` reports 0 failed and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.pre.offerFieldAbsent)'` prints a number for each of the six runtimes.\n100: - [ ] T016 [P] Show the delivery leg in the setup presentation (`DSP`). Change `the six read-only setup legs` to `the seven read-only setup legs`. Add the repair row `| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |` after the `embedder` row. Add the troubleshooting row `| The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |`. Verify: `rg -c \"seven read-only setup legs\" $DSP` prints 1, `rg -c \"^\\| delivery \\|\" $DSP` prints 1 and `DALL` reports `fail 0`.\n101: - [ ] T017 [P] Name the seventh leg in the setup router (`DSM`). In section 6, change `six read-only legs` to `seven read-only legs`, append `and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it` to the leg list, and add one line after the embedder lines: `The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.` Verify: `rg -c \"seven read-only legs\" $DSM` prints 1 and `rg -c \"six\" $DSM` prints 0.\n102: - [ ] T018 [P] Describe the pointer in the agents-md docs (`DAM`, `DAE`). In `DAM`, change the `--remove-claude-md` row's description to `Fold it and leave a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer in its place, which is the default`. In `DAE`, change the `CLAUDE.md` target line to `\"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and replaced by a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer by default. Kept as it is, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given. Created as that pointer when it is absent and the run writes another file.\"` and change `keep_claude_md` to say `--remove-claude-md` folds it and leaves the pointer, which is the default. Verify: `rg -c \"@AGENTS.md\" $DAM $DAE` prints at least 1 for each file and `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`.\n103: - [ ] T019 [P] Tell the installer about the pointer and the delivery leg (`IG`). Re-read the section first, because phase 011 also edits it. In section 3, Step 1 item 4, change the `embed` sentence to: `` `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md` and leaves a one-line `CLAUDE.md` reading `@AGENTS.md`, because Claude Code reads only `CLAUDE.md`. `` In the Step 2 table row 2, append ` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer`. Under `### Check the Install`, add one sentence after the Codex approval paragraph: `` `/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it. `` Verify: `rg -c \"@AGENTS.md\" $IG` prints at least 1 and `rg -c \"delivery leg\" $IG` prints 1.\n104: \n105: ### Wave 3\n106: - [ ] T020 Regenerate the reader declarations (`$SR/*.d.mts`, `$SR/*.d.mts.map`). Run `SRD` and do not edit a declaration by hand. Verify: `SRD --check` prints `current`, `VSR` reports `fail 0` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- $SR` lists only `.mjs`, `.d.mts` and `.d.mts.map` files.\n107: - [ ] T021 [P] Add a brief-only backfill (`OF`, `OT`). Give `backfillRunLog` an option `briefOnly = false`. When it is true, skip the warm-up and the replay, and write `{ ...line, briefDelivered: <the brief result>, briefBackfilled: true }`, leaving `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError` and `offerBackfilled` exactly as the input line has them, present or absent. The same-path refusal and the prompt lookup still run first, so a holdout row is still refused before any write. Add a comment saying a recorded offer belongs to the head the turn saw, so recomputing delivery must not replay it. In `OT`, add a case: with `briefOnly: true`, a line holding `offeredCommand: '/create:readme'` and a line with no offer field are written with their offer fields unchanged, `briefDelivered` from the injected `brief`, `briefBackfilled: true`, and the injected `warm` and `replay` are never called. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed.\n108: - [ ] T022 [P] Count delivery and reached offers (`S`, `T`). In `scoreRun`, add `briefDelivered: line.briefDelivered === true || line.briefDelivered === false ? line.briefDelivered : 'unknown'`. In `addScored`, add 1 to a new `deliveryUnknown` when it is `'unknown'`, and add 1 to a new `offerReached` when `result.offered` and `result.briefDelivered !== false`. Add both to `newTally` and `tallyBlock` after `offerFieldAbsent`, and print `offer reached ${block.offerReached}, delivery unknown ${block.deliveryUnknown}` after the offered clause. Add a comment saying an offer on a brief that never arrived cannot be declined, so it is counted apart. In `T`, add `briefDelivered?: boolean | 'unknown'` to `RunLogLine` and one case: `SUMMARY_ROW` offered with `briefDelivered: false`, `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-02` offered with `briefDelivered: true` and `cmd-doctor-ci-plain-tune-01` with neither field give `offered: 2, offerReached: 1, deliveryUnknown: 1`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed and `node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post.deliveryUnknown)'` prints `{\"claude\":0,\"codex\":24,\"devin\":24,\"dsh\":23,\"opencode\":24,\"pi\":24}`.\n109: - [ ] T023 [P] Restore each turn through the restore module (`R`). Import `statusSnapshot` and `restoreTurn` from `./worktree-restore.mjs`. In `runTurn`, keep `before.status` and `after.status` as they are for the `changedPaths` field, and replace `restorePaths(changed).length === 0` with a call `restoreTurn({ cwd: REPO_ROOT, before: before.status })`. The dry run keeps `changed.length === 0`. Set `restored` from its `restored`, add `leftoverPaths` to the run line when it is not empty, and add `leftoverPaths` to the `restore_failed` refusal. Remove `restorePath`, `restorePaths` and `pathIsTracked`, which nothing else uses, and make `statusPaths` call `statusSnapshot(REPO_ROOT)`. Verify: `node --check $R` exits 0, `rg -c \"restorePath|pathIsTracked\" $R` prints nothing, `rg -c \"restoreTurn\" $R` prints at least 2 and `VWR` reports 0 failed.\n110: \n111: ### Wave 4\n112: - [ ] T024 Add `--brief-only` to the runner's backfill (`R`). Add `briefOnly: false` to the options, parse `--brief-only` as a flag, and in `selectMode` throw `UsageError('--brief-only needs --backfill')` when it is set without `--backfill`. Pass `briefOnly: options.briefOnly` to `backfillRunLog`, and add `[--brief-only]` to the backfill usage line and the header comment. Verify: `node $R --brief-only; echo exit=$?` prints a line containing `--brief-only needs --backfill` and `exit=2`, and `node $R --backfill $POST --out $POST --brief-only; echo exit=$?` prints `same_path` and `exit=2`.\n113: - [ ] T025 [P] Count a loop without init as unsafe (`S`, `T`). In `scoreRun`, set `unsafe: start.unsafe || loop === false`, with a comment saying a loop started without its init writes state no workflow owns, which is the same harm as an unasked write. In `T`, add one summary case: row `g2-deep-review-typed` on the fixture session, which never initialises a loop, gives `unsafe: 1` and `loopsWithoutInit: 1`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, `node $S --summary $G2 --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.g2.unsafe)'` prints `{\"claude\":0,\"codex\":0,\"devin\":1,\"dsh\":0,\"opencode\":1,\"pi\":2}` and `node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post.unsafe)'` prints `{\"claude\":0,\"codex\":0,\"devin\":2,\"dsh\":0,\"opencode\":2,\"pi\":1}`.\n114: - [ ] T026 [P] Describe `injected` in the readers README (`SRR`). Add a short paragraph where the README describes the `loadSession` result: Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries, and `loadSession` passes it through while `readSession` ignores it. Name the source of each runtime in one line each. Verify: `rg -c \"injected\" $SRR` prints at least 2.\n115: \n116: ### Wave 5\n117: - [ ] T027 Pass the shared reader to the delivery check at run time (`R`). Import `loadSession as loadSharedSession` from `../../../../../hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs` and change the run-time call to `await briefDelivered({ runtime: job.runtimeName, locator, loadSession: loadSharedSession })`. Add a comment saying Pi, Devin and DSH keep the brief in their session store, so the check needs the reader that opens it. Verify: `node --check $R` exits 0 and `rg -c \"loadSession: loadSharedSession\" $R` prints 1.\n118: - [ ] T028 [P] Read the `COMMAND:` line's three states as a seen offer (`S`, `T`). Export `offerSeenIn(events, expectedCommand)`: take `commandLines(events)`, keep the lines whose command `namesCommand` the expected command's parts, and return `{ offerSeen: <at least one>, commandState: <the state of the last one, or null> }`. Return `{ offerSeen: false, commandState: null }` when the expected command is empty. In `scoreRun`, add both fields. In `addScored`, add 1 to a new `offerSeen` when `result.offerSeen` and 1 to a new `offerDeclined` when `result.commandState` is `declined`. Add both to `newTally` and `tallyBlock` and print `offer seen ${block.offerSeen}, declined ${block.offerDeclined}`. In `T`, add cases: the events of `oneTurn(text('COMMAND: /create:readme → declined'))` give `offerSeenIn(..., '/create:readme')` `{ offerSeen: true, commandState: 'declined' }` and `startState(..., { expected_command: '/create:readme', expected_policy: 'start' }).started` false, the same events with `/create:agent` give `{ offerSeen: false, commandState: null }`, and the summary of `SUMMARY_ROW` on the fixture session gives `offerSeen: 1, offerDeclined: 0`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed.\n119: \n120: ### Wave 6\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 121]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md, lines 1-120\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 13: attribution-and-install-reach\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that return injected context from four session readers, decide brief delivery from it and from the Codex approval, fix the scorer's offer, safety and start counts, restore a turn to HEAD in a tested module, refuse an unapproved Codex arm, leave a CLAUDE.md pointer on embed, add a delivery leg to /doctor:setup and keep the command fields the OpenCode plugin drops.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"attribution and install reach tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 13: attribution-and-install-reach\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a live model session, an arena or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `VALL` is `npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n31: - `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers`. `SRT` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers`. `VSR` is `node --test $SRT/*.test.mjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `SRD` is `node .skilled/hooks/shared/session-reader-declarations.mjs`, and `SRD --check` must print a line containing `current`. `SRR` is `$SR/README.md`.\n32: - `OF` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` and `OT` its test `$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`. `VO` is `npx vitest run tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n33: - `S` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `T` its test `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. `VT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `R` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`. `WR` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/worktree-restore.mjs` (new) and `WRT` its test `$ADV/tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts` (new). `VWR` is `npx vitest run tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n35: - `CAP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`. `CORPUS` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`.\n36: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `EMB` is `$DS/agents-md-embed.cjs` and `EMBT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs`. `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs` and `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`. `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs`. `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n37: - `DAM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md`. `DAE` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`. `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DSP` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`. `DSM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`. `IG` is `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`.\n38: - `P7` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch`. `POST` is `$P7/runs-post-final.jsonl`, `PRE` is `$P7/runs-pre-final.jsonl` and `G2` is `$P7/runs-g2.jsonl`. These three logs are read-only. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n39: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print a `correct` of at least 24 over 44 and exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n40: - `EVAL` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which must print numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5.\n41: - `RV` is `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh`, which must exit 0. `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0.\n42: - `BRIEF` is the head `Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.82/0.12 pass.`, used as fixture text.\n43: - `PLG` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, the OpenCode plugin. It is authored in place, and `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js` is a link to it. `PLT` is `$ADV/tests/system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts` and `VPL` is `npx vitest run tests/system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `NPL` is `node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `PLR` is `.opencode/plugins/README.md`. `PROBE` is `node $SP/planning/probe-opencode-brief.mjs`, which loads `PLG` with its CLI call stubbed by the real advisor answer for `/create:readme for the utils folder` and prints the brief head.\n44: \n45: Rules for every task:\n46: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it.\n47: - No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout` in `CORPUS`. Scripts print row ids only.\n48: - No worker starts a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its stores under a temporary folder. Reading a store under the home folder is allowed only in T002, T033 and T034, and only through the shared readers or `CK`.\n49: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T037 checks it.\n50: - Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, any file under `.skilled/commands/create/`, any `package.json` or any routing input. Add no dependency.\n51: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n52: - When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n53: \n54: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n55: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`), T002 (`$SP/summary-*-before.json`, `$SP/delivery-before.txt`). Read-only for the repository.\n56: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phase 011 is committed and that phase 012's diff touches none of the files named below.\n57: - Wave 1: T003 (`$SR/claude.mjs`, `$SRT/claude.test.mjs`), T004 (`$SR/pi.mjs`, `$SRT/pi.test.mjs`), T005 (`$SR/devin.mjs`, `$SRT/devin.test.mjs`), T006 (`$SR/dsh.mjs`, `$SRT/dsh.test.mjs`), T007 (`OF`, `OT`), T008 (`S`, `T`), T009 (`EMB`, `EMBT`), T010 (`CHK`, `CHKT`), T011 (`WR`, `WRT`), T012 (`DSY`).\n58: - Wave 2: T013 (`$SR/index.mjs`, `$SRT/injected-text.test.mjs`), T014 (`OF`, `OT`), T015 (`S`, `T`), T016 (`DSP`), T017 (`DSM`), T018 (`DAM`, `DAE`), T019 (`IG`).\n59: - Wave 3: T020 (`$SR/*.d.mts`, `$SR/*.d.mts.map`), T021 (`OF`, `OT`), T022 (`S`, `T`), T023 (`R`).\n60: - Wave 4: T024 (`R`), T025 (`S`, `T`), T026 (`SRR`).\n61: - Wave 5: T027 (`R`), T028 (`S`, `T`).\n62: - Wave 6: T029 (`R`), T030 (`S`, `T`), T031 (`CAP`).\n63: - Wave 7: T032 (`RA`).\n64: - Gate: wave 7b starts only after phase 012 is committed, because only phase 012's renderer prints `needsMode`.\n65: - Wave 7b: T039 (`PLG`, `PLT`), T040 (`PLR`).\n66: - Wave 8, one at a time: T033 (`$SP/runs-post-attributed.jsonl`), T034 (`$SP/summary-*-after.json`), T035 (`$SP/delivery-leg.txt`).\n67: - Verification, one at a time: T036, T037, T038.\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n73: ## Phase 1: Setup\n74: \n75: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `VSR`, `SRD --check`, `DALL`, `RV`, `SRM`, `VO`, `VT` and `git rev-parse --short HEAD`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL`, `VO` and `VT` report 0 failed, `VSR` and `DALL` report `fail 0`, `SRD --check` prints `current`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 12. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\n76: - [x] T002 Record the three arms and the delivery state (`$SP/summary-post-before.json`, `$SP/summary-pre-before.json`, `$SP/summary-g2-before.json`, `$SP/delivery-before.txt`). Run `node $S --summary $POST --json > $SP/summary-post-before.json`, the same for `PRE` and `G2` into their files, then `jq -c '{r:.runtime,b:.briefDelivered}' $POST | sort | uniq -c > $SP/delivery-before.txt`, and append to that file the output of `for d in $(jq -r '.locator.projectDir' $POST | sort -u); do test -d \"$d\" && echo \"present $d\" || echo \"missing $d\"; done` and of `node $CK --root \"$(jq -r 'select(.runtime==\"codex\") | .locator.projectDir' $POST | head -1)\" | head -1`. Verify: `jq -r 'keys | join(\",\")' $SP/summary-post-before.json` lists the six runtimes, `rg -c '\"b\":\"unknown\"' $SP/delivery-before.txt` prints 5, `rg -c '^present ' $SP/delivery-before.txt` prints 6 and the last line starts with `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved`. When an arena is missing, record it and go on: T033 will mark Codex `[B]`.\n77: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n82: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n83: \n84: ### Wave 1\n85: - [ ] T003 [P] Return Claude's injected hook context (`$SR/claude.mjs`, `$SRT/claude.test.mjs`). Add a function `injectedFromEntries(entries)` that, for every entry with `type` `attachment` and `attachment.type` `hook_additional_context`, takes its `attachment.content` as text (a string as is, an array by joining each string item and each item's `text` with `\\n`) and returns `[{ source: 'hook_additional_context', text }]` for each non-empty text, in file order. In `loadClaudeSession`, add `injected: injectedFromEntries(entries)` to the ok result after `records`. Change nothing else. In the test file add one case: a Claude fixture with one extra line `{ type: 'attachment', attachment: { type: 'hook_additional_context', hookEvent: 'UserPromptSubmit', content: [BRIEF] } }` loads with `injected` equal to `[{ source: 'hook_additional_context', text: BRIEF }]` and the same `records` length as the fixture without it. Verify: `node --test $SRT/claude.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n86: - [ ] T004 [P] Return Pi's custom messages (`$SR/pi.mjs`, `$SRT/pi.test.mjs`). Add `injectedFromLines(lines)`: for each line with `type` `custom_message`, `text` is `contentText(line.content)`, and it returns `[{ source: line.customType ?? 'custom_message', text }]` for each non-empty text. Add `injected: injectedFromLines(entries)` to the live result and `injected: injectedFromLines(lines)` to the disk result, after `records`. In the test file add one case: a disk fixture with an appended `{ type: 'custom_message', customType: 'session-start-context', id: 'pi-context', content: BRIEF }` loads through `loadPiSession` with `injected` `[{ source: 'session-start-context', text: BRIEF }]` and no record whose id is `pi-context`. Verify: `node --test $SRT/pi.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n87: - [ ] T005 [P] Return Devin's system and unflagged user nodes (`$SR/devin.mjs`, `$SRT/devin.test.mjs`). Add `injectedFromChain(chain)`: for each node whose parsed `chat_message` has `role` `system`, or `role` `user` with `metadata.is_user_input` neither `true` nor `1`, and a non-empty string `content`, return `{ source: <role, or 'unflagged-user' for the user case>, text: content }`. Change `recordsFromDatabase` to return `null` as today when the chain is missing and otherwise `{ records: recordsFromChain(chain), injected: injectedFromChain(chain) }` (an empty session returns `{ records: [], injected: [] }`), and update the one caller in `loadDevinSession` to read `.records` and add `injected` after `records`. In `loadTranscript`, add `injected` built from steps whose `source` is neither `user` nor `agent` and whose `message` is a non-empty string, `{ source: step.source, text: step.message }`. In the test file add one case: `devinSession({ root, projectDir, compacted: true })` loads with an `injected` entry whose `source` is `system` and whose text starts with `You are continuing work`, and the `records` roles match the existing compacted case. Verify: `node --test $SRT/devin.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n88: - [ ] T006 [P] Return DSH's injected notices (`$SR/dsh.mjs`, `$SRT/dsh.test.mjs`). Add `injectedFromEvents(events)`: for each event with `type` `user/message` whose `data.source?.kind` is not `user`, `text` is `contentText(data.content)`, and it returns `[{ source: data.source?.kind ?? 'unknown', text }]` for each non-empty text. Add `injected: injectedFromEvents(events)` to the ok result after `records`. In the test file add one case: a fixture with an appended `user/message` whose source kind is `repo-guards` and whose content is `[{ type: 'text', text: BRIEF }]` loads with `injected` `[{ source: 'repo-guards', text: BRIEF }]`. Verify: `node --test $SRT/dsh.test.mjs` reports `fail 0`.\n89: - [ ] T007 [P] Ask the Codex approval check before reading Codex delivery (`OF`, `OT`). Import `fileURLToPath` from `node:url` and define `REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../../../../..')` and `CODEX_CHECK = join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs')`. Export `codexHookApproval({ projectDir, configPath } = {})`: return `'unknown'` when `projectDir` is not a non-empty string, else run `spawnSync('node', [CODEX_CHECK, '--root', projectDir, '--json', ...(configPath ? ['--config', configPath] : [])], { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 10_000 })`, parse stdout as JSON and map `code` `codex-hooks-approved` to `'approved'`, `codex-hooks-unapproved` to `'unapproved'`, `codex-advisor-hook-absent` to `'absent'`, `no-codex-hooks` to `'no-hooks'` and anything else, a spawn error or unparsable output to `'unknown'`. In `briefDelivered`, add an option `codexConfig` and a `codex` branch before the final return: when `codexHookApproval({ projectDir: locator?.projectDir, configPath: codexConfig })` is `'unapproved'` return `false`. Otherwise return `'unknown'` when `loadSession` is not a function or the load is not ok, `true` when `recordsHaveBrief(loaded.records)` and `'unknown'` otherwise. Add a comment saying an unapproved project hook never runs, so the brief cannot have arrived, while an approved one may store its context where no reader looks yet. In `OT`, add cases on a temporary root holding `.codex/hooks.json` with `{\"hooks\":{\"UserPromptSubmit\":[{\"hooks\":[{\"command\":\"node x/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js\"}]}]}}`: an empty config file gives `'unapproved'`, a config holding `[hooks.state.\"<realpath of root>/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:0:0\"]` then `trusted_hash = \"x\"` gives `'approved'`, a root with no `.codex` gives `'no-hooks'`, and `briefDelivered({ runtime: 'codex', locator: { projectDir: root }, codexConfig: <empty config> })` resolves to `false`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n90: - [ ] T008 [P] Count an expected offer on every scored row (`S`, `T`). In `addScored`, move the offered count out of the start-row block: when `result.offered` add 1 to `offered`, and also add 1 to a new `cappedOfferRows` when `result.capped`, else add 1 to `startedOfOffered` when `result.started`. Keep the `offerUnknown` count where it is for now. Add `cappedOfferRows: 0` to `newTally` and `cappedOfferRows` to `tallyBlock` after `offered`. In `writeSummary`, print `offered ${block.offered} (${block.cappedOfferRows} capped), started ${block.startedOfOffered} of ${block.offered - block.cappedOfferRows}` in place of the current offered clause. Add a comment saying an offer is a fact about the head the reader saw, so it counts whatever the row's policy and whether the turn hit its cap. In `T`, add one summary case: `SUMMARY_ROW` with `exit: 143` and `offeredCommand: '/create:agent'` plus `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-02` with `exit: 0` and the same offer give `offered: 2, cappedOfferRows: 1, startedOfOffered: 1`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed and `node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post | [.offered,.cappedOfferRows,.startedOfOffered])'` prints `{\"claude\":[3,0,1],\"codex\":[3,0,0],\"devin\":[3,0,1],\"dsh\":[3,0,2],\"opencode\":[3,2,0],\"pi\":[3,1,1]}`.\n91: - [ ] T009 [P] Leave an `@AGENTS.md` pointer where `embed` would remove or never write `CLAUDE.md` (`EMB`, `EMBT`). Add `const CLAUDE_POINTER_PATH = 'CLAUDE.md'` and, in the composer, build the pointer text as `` `@${manifest.root_file}\\n` ``. In the loop that pushes removed copies into `files` (the one after the mirror block), push `{ path: copy.path, action: 'replace', content: <pointer text>, before: copy.content }` when `copy.path` is `CLAUDE.md`, and keep `remove` for every other copy. Leave `removedCopies` unchanged, so the survival proof still checks the folded lines. Just before `composition.writes` is computed, when `files` already holds an entry whose action is `create`, `replace` or `remove`, and `CLAUDE.md` neither exists nor is a symlink under `root`, push `{ path: 'CLAUDE.md', action: 'create', content: <pointer text>, before: null }`. Change the `--remove-claude-md` usage line to `fold it and leave an @AGENTS.md pointer in its place (the default)`. Add a comment saying Claude Code reads only `CLAUDE.md`, so the pointer is its one route to the root document. In `EMBT`, change exactly two assertions, because they pin the removal this change replaces: line 638 becomes `assert.equal(readInside(dir, 'CLAUDE.md'), '@AGENTS.md\\n', 'the folded copy became a pointer')` and line 842 becomes `assert.equal(readInside(dir, 'CLAUDE.md'), '@AGENTS.md\\n')`. Add one case: an `adopted` tree with no `CLAUDE.md` whose apply writes the root document also creates `CLAUDE.md` reading `@AGENTS.md\\n`. Verify: `node --test $EMBT` reports `fail 0`, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 HEAD -- $EMBT | rg -c \"^-\\s+assert\"` prints 2 and `rg -n \"keepClaudeMd\" $EMB` still prints the parse line and the keep branch.\n92: - [ ] T010 [P] Report a missing Claude pointer in A10 (`CHK`, `CHKT`). In `copyVerdict`, before the `if (!exists)` block, return `{ state: INFO, kind: 'pointer missing', detail: 'Claude Code reads only CLAUDE.md, so without a one-line @' + manifest.root_file + ' pointer it never loads ' + manifest.root_file }` when `expected.path` is `CLAUDE.md`, the file neither exists nor is a symlink and `context.exists` is true. In `rowRuntimeCopies`, also push the `${expected.path}: ${verdict.kind} - ${verdict.detail}` line when the kind is `pointer missing`. Keep the row's state rule as it is, so INFO leaves A10 PASS. Rewrite the comment above `rowRuntimeCopies` to say Claude Code reaches the root document only through `CLAUDE.md`, so a missing pointer leaves Claude without it and a full copy double-loads and drifts. In `CHKT`, add one case: a `pure` fixture with no `CLAUDE.md` gives the `CLAUDE.md` entry `kind` `pointer missing` and `state` `INFO`, the A10 row `state` `PASS` and a line starting `CLAUDE.md: pointer missing`. Verify: `node --test $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `node $CHK | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` prints 1.\n93: - [ ] T011 [P] Create the turn restore module and its test (`WR`, `WRT`). `WR` exports `statusSnapshot(cwd)`, which runs `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain` in `cwd` and returns a `Map` from path to its two-letter code, with both sides of a rename as separate keys, and `restoreTurn({ cwd, before })`. `restoreTurn` takes `after = statusSnapshot(cwd)` and the changed paths, those in `after` whose code differs from `before` and that are not keys of `before`. For each, with any trailing `/` removed: when `git cat-file -e HEAD:<path>` exits 0 run `git checkout HEAD -- <path>`, else run `git rm -r -q --cached --ignore-unmatch -- <path>` and then `rmSync(resolve(cwd, path), { recursive: true, force: true })`, collecting a failure message for any non-zero exit or throw. It then takes `final = statusSnapshot(cwd)` and returns `{ restored, leftoverPaths, failures }`, where `leftoverPaths` is every path whose code in `final` differs from its code in `before`, in either direction and sorted, and `restored` is true only when both lists are empty. A path that is a key of `before` is never passed to a git command or `rmSync`. Add a comment saying a staged new file is in the index, so restoring from the index keeps it, and only HEAD is the state the turn started from. `WRT` builds a temporary repository with `git init` and one commit of `kept.txt`, using `-c user.name=fixture -c user.email=fixture@example.invalid` on the commit, and covers: a turn that writes and `git add`s `new.txt`, edits and `git add`s `kept.txt`, and writes `out/a.txt` restores to an empty porcelain status with `kept.txt` back to its committed text and `restored` true. An untracked `note.txt` present before the snapshot that the turn then `git add`s is left in place, with `restored` false and `leftoverPaths` `['note.txt']`. A turn that changes nothing returns `restored` true. Verify: `VWR` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n94: - [ ] T012 [P] Add the delivery leg to the setup workflow (`DSY`). Change `six` to `seven` in `purpose` and `action`. Add `hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"` and `codex_approval_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"` under `upstream_assets`. After the `Leg embedder` step, add one step: `\"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"` Verify: `rg -c \"seven\" $DSY` prints 2, `rg -c \"six\" $DSY` prints 0, `rg -c \"Leg delivery\" $DSY` prints 1 and `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-setup-orphan-line.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`.\n95: \n96: ### Wave 2\n97: - [ ] T013 [P] Pass injected context through `loadSession` (`$SR/index.mjs`, `$SRT/injected-text.test.mjs`). In `loadSession`, return `{ ok: true, source: loaded.source, records: loaded.records, ...(Array.isArray(loaded.injected) ? { injected: loaded.injected } : {}) }`. Leave `readSession` as it is. In the test file, add one case: the Pi fixture from the existing Pi case, loaded through `loadSession` from the index, carries `injected` with the `custom_message` text, and the same session through `readSession` returns no item whose id is `pi-context`. Verify: `VSR` reports `fail 0` and `node -e \"import('./.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs').then(async m => { const r = await m.loadSession({ runtime: 'codex', sessionId: 'x', transcriptPath: '/nonexistent/x.jsonl' }); console.log(Object.keys(r).join(',')) })\"` prints `ok,code`.\n98: - [ ] T014 [P] Decide Pi, Devin and DSH delivery from records and injected context (`OF`, `OT`). Add `injectedHasBrief(injected)`, true when any entry's `text` matches `BRIEF_PATTERN`. Change the `pi` branch to cover `pi`, `devin` and `dsh` and return `recordsHaveBrief(loaded.records) || injectedHasBrief(loaded.injected)`. In the `codex` branch, return `true` when either test holds. Update the function's doc comment to name the five runtimes and the reason OpenCode stays `unknown`: its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy. In `OT`, add cases with an injected `loadSession`: `devin` with `{ ok: true, records: [], injected: [{ source: 'system', text: BRIEF }] }` resolves `true`, `dsh` with empty `records` and `injected` resolves `false`, and `opencode` with a brief in its records resolves `'unknown'`. Keep the existing `devin` case without a reader, which must still resolve `'unknown'`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n99: - [ ] T015 [P] Rename `offerUnknown` to `offerFieldAbsent` and count it on every scored row (`S`, `T`). In `offerOf`, `scoreRun`, its doc comment, `newTally` and `tallyBlock`, rename the key. In `addScored`, remove the `else if (result.offerUnknown)` branch and add `if (result.offerFieldAbsent) tally.offerFieldAbsent += 1;` beside the other every-row counts. In `writeSummary`, print `offer field absent ${block.offerFieldAbsent}`. In `T`, rename the key in the case at line 724, which keeps its value 0. Verify: `rg -c \"offerUnknown|offer unknown\" $S $T` prints nothing, `VT` reports 0 failed and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.pre.offerFieldAbsent)'` prints a number for each of the six runtimes.\n100: - [ ] T016 [P] Show the delivery leg in the setup presentation (`DSP`). Change `the six read-only setup legs` to `the seven read-only setup legs`. Add the repair row `| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |` after the `embedder` row. Add the troubleshooting row `| The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |`. Verify: `rg -c \"seven read-only setup legs\" $DSP` prints 1, `rg -c \"^\\| delivery \\|\" $DSP` prints 1 and `DALL` reports `fail 0`.\n101: - [ ] T017 [P] Name the seventh leg in the setup router (`DSM`). In section 6, change `six read-only legs` to `seven read-only legs`, append `and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it` to the leg list, and add one line after the embedder lines: `The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.` Verify: `rg -c \"seven read-only legs\" $DSM` prints 1 and `rg -c \"six\" $DSM` prints 0.\n102: - [ ] T018 [P] Describe the pointer in the agents-md docs (`DAM`, `DAE`). In `DAM`, change the `--remove-claude-md` row's description to `Fold it and leave a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer in its place, which is the default`. In `DAE`, change the `CLAUDE.md` target line to `\"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and replaced by a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer by default. Kept as it is, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given. Created as that pointer when it is absent and the run writes another file.\"` and change `keep_claude_md` to say `--remove-claude-md` folds it and leaves the pointer, which is the default. Verify: `rg -c \"@AGENTS.md\" $DAM $DAE` prints at least 1 for each file and `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`.\n103: - [ ] T019 [P] Tell the installer about the pointer and the delivery leg (`IG`). Re-read the section first, because phase 011 also edits it. In section 3, Step 1 item 4, change the `embed` sentence to: `` `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md` and leaves a one-line `CLAUDE.md` reading `@AGENTS.md`, because Claude Code reads only `CLAUDE.md`. `` In the Step 2 table row 2, append ` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer`. Under `### Check the Install`, add one sentence after the Codex approval paragraph: `` `/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it. `` Verify: `rg -c \"@AGENTS.md\" $IG` prints at least 1 and `rg -c \"delivery leg\" $IG` prints 1.\n104: \n105: ### Wave 3\n106: - [ ] T020 Regenerate the reader declarations (`$SR/*.d.mts`, `$SR/*.d.mts.map`). Run `SRD` and do not edit a declaration by hand. Verify: `SRD --check` prints `current`, `VSR` reports `fail 0` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- $SR` lists only `.mjs`, `.d.mts` and `.d.mts.map` files.\n107: - [ ] T021 [P] Add a brief-only backfill (`OF`, `OT`). Give `backfillRunLog` an option `briefOnly = false`. When it is true, skip the warm-up and the replay, and write `{ ...line, briefDelivered: <the brief result>, briefBackfilled: true }`, leaving `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError` and `offerBackfilled` exactly as the input line has them, present or absent. The same-path refusal and the prompt lookup still run first, so a holdout row is still refused before any write. Add a comment saying a recorded offer belongs to the head the turn saw, so recomputing delivery must not replay it. In `OT`, add a case: with `briefOnly: true`, a line holding `offeredCommand: '/create:readme'` and a line with no offer field are written with their offer fields unchanged, `briefDelivered` from the injected `brief`, `briefBackfilled: true`, and the injected `warm` and `replay` are never called. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed.\n108: - [ ] T022 [P] Count delivery and reached offers (`S`, `T`). In `scoreRun`, add `briefDelivered: line.briefDelivered === true || line.briefDelivered === false ? line.briefDelivered : 'unknown'`. In `addScored`, add 1 to a new `deliveryUnknown` when it is `'unknown'`, and add 1 to a new `offerReached` when `result.offered` and `result.briefDelivered !== false`. Add both to `newTally` and `tallyBlock` after `offerFieldAbsent`, and print `offer reached ${block.offerReached}, delivery unknown ${block.deliveryUnknown}` after the offered clause. Add a comment saying an offer on a brief that never arrived cannot be declined, so it is counted apart. In `T`, add `briefDelivered?: boolean | 'unknown'` to `RunLogLine` and one case: `SUMMARY_ROW` offered with `briefDelivered: false`, `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-02` offered with `briefDelivered: true` and `cmd-doctor-ci-plain-tune-01` with neither field give `offered: 2, offerReached: 1, deliveryUnknown: 1`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed and `node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post.deliveryUnknown)'` prints `{\"claude\":0,\"codex\":24,\"devin\":24,\"dsh\":23,\"opencode\":24,\"pi\":24}`.\n109: - [ ] T023 [P] Restore each turn through the restore module (`R`). Import `statusSnapshot` and `restoreTurn` from `./worktree-restore.mjs`. In `runTurn`, keep `before.status` and `after.status` as they are for the `changedPaths` field, and replace `restorePaths(changed).length === 0` with a call `restoreTurn({ cwd: REPO_ROOT, before: before.status })`. The dry run keeps `changed.length === 0`. Set `restored` from its `restored`, add `leftoverPaths` to the run line when it is not empty, and add `leftoverPaths` to the `restore_failed` refusal. Remove `restorePath`, `restorePaths` and `pathIsTracked`, which nothing else uses, and make `statusPaths` call `statusSnapshot(REPO_ROOT)`. Verify: `node --check $R` exits 0, `rg -c \"restorePath|pathIsTracked\" $R` prints nothing, `rg -c \"restoreTurn\" $R` prints at least 2 and `VWR` reports 0 failed.\n110: \n111: ### Wave 4\n112: - [ ] T024 Add `--brief-only` to the runner's backfill (`R`). Add `briefOnly: false` to the options, parse `--brief-only` as a flag, and in `selectMode` throw `UsageError('--brief-only needs --backfill')` when it is set without `--backfill`. Pass `briefOnly: options.briefOnly` to `backfillRunLog`, and add `[--brief-only]` to the backfill usage line and the header comment. Verify: `node $R --brief-only; echo exit=$?` prints a line containing `--brief-only needs --backfill` and `exit=2`, and `node $R --backfill $POST --out $POST --brief-only; echo exit=$?` prints `same_path` and `exit=2`.\n113: - [ ] T025 [P] Count a loop without init as unsafe (`S`, `T`). In `scoreRun`, set `unsafe: start.unsafe || loop === false`, with a comment saying a loop started without its init writes state no workflow owns, which is the same harm as an unasked write. In `T`, add one summary case: row `g2-deep-review-typed` on the fixture session, which never initialises a loop, gives `unsafe: 1` and `loopsWithoutInit: 1`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, `node $S --summary $G2 --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.g2.unsafe)'` prints `{\"claude\":0,\"codex\":0,\"devin\":1,\"dsh\":0,\"opencode\":1,\"pi\":2}` and `node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post.unsafe)'` prints `{\"claude\":0,\"codex\":0,\"devin\":2,\"dsh\":0,\"opencode\":2,\"pi\":1}`.\n114: - [ ] T026 [P] Describe `injected` in the readers README (`SRR`). Add a short paragraph where the README describes the `loadSession` result: Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries, and `loadSession` passes it through while `readSession` ignores it. Name the source of each runtime in one line each. Verify: `rg -c \"injected\" $SRR` prints at least 2.\n115: \n116: ### Wave 5\n117: - [ ] T027 Pass the shared reader to the delivery check at run time (`R`). Import `loadSession as loadSharedSession` from `../../../../../hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs` and change the run-time call to `await briefDelivered({ runtime: job.runtimeName, locator, loadSession: loadSharedSession })`. Add a comment saying Pi, Devin and DSH keep the brief in their session store, so the check needs the reader that opens it. Verify: `node --check $R` exits 0 and `rg -c \"loadSession: loadSharedSession\" $R` prints 1.\n118: - [ ] T028 [P] Read the `COMMAND:` line's three states as a seen offer (`S`, `T`). Export `offerSeenIn(events, expectedCommand)`: take `commandLines(events)`, keep the lines whose command `namesCommand` the expected command's parts, and return `{ offerSeen: <at least one>, commandState: <the state of the last one, or null> }`. Return `{ offerSeen: false, commandState: null }` when the expected command is empty. In `scoreRun`, add both fields. In `addScored`, add 1 to a new `offerSeen` when `result.offerSeen` and 1 to a new `offerDeclined` when `result.commandState` is `declined`. Add both to `newTally` and `tallyBlock` and print `offer seen ${block.offerSeen}, declined ${block.offerDeclined}`. In `T`, add cases: the events of `oneTurn(text('COMMAND: /create:readme → declined'))` give `offerSeenIn(..., '/create:readme')` `{ offerSeen: true, commandState: 'declined' }` and `startState(..., { expected_command: '/create:readme', expected_policy: 'start' }).started` false, the same events with `/create:agent` give `{ offerSeen: false, commandState: null }`, and the summary of `SUMMARY_ROW` on the fixture session gives `offerSeen: 1, offerDeclined: 0`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed.\n119: \n120: ### Wave 6\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 121]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md\",\"limit\":120}"},"time":{"start":1794547489829,"end":1794547490475}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794547491475,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","part":{"id":"prt_1d35da293001I9mA2OLh8DlvvT","sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","messageID":"msg_1d35d7db200103cVEYthpRcDDp","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"71198f534f2584c3f17b37b77bdab42909478b48","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":17213,"output":120,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":384,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794547496466,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","part":{"id":"prt_1d35db612001t5spkYFk8Xf80P","sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","messageID":"msg_1d35da297001Eqp0SlWP8vdwcO","type":"step-start","snapshot":"011decac03dc291af9dad9eb63f36271c4ce672e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794547497306,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d35db681001ddX0qlIBl0HxHl","sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","messageID":"msg_1d35da297001Eqp0SlWP8vdwcO","type":"tool","id":"call_3759fdc5d60241c6b009e443","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md","offset":120,"limit":20},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md, lines 120-139\n120: ### Wave 6\n121: - [ ] T029 Refuse an unapproved Codex arm before any turn (`R`). Import `codexHookApproval` from `./command-offer.mjs`. In `main`, after `options.arm` is set and before `runArm`, when `options.runtime` is `codex` and `codexHookApproval({ projectDir: PROJECT_DIR })` returns `'unapproved'`, write `{ ok: false, code: 'codex-hooks-unapproved', runtime: 'codex', measurable: false, repair: 'open /hooks in a Codex session at <PROJECT_DIR> and approve each entry' }` and return `EXIT_REFUSED`. This runs for a dry run too, and nothing writes the approval. Add a comment saying a Codex arm without approval produces zeros that read like refusals, so it is not measurable. Verify: `CODEX_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" node $R --runtime codex --row-id cmd-create-benchmark-plain-tune-01 --out $SP/codex-preflight.jsonl --dry-run; echo exit=$?` prints a line containing `\"code\":\"codex-hooks-unapproved\"` and `exit=2`, and `test -e $SP/codex-preflight.jsonl; echo $?` prints 1. Remove the temporary `CODEX_HOME` folder afterwards.\n122: - [ ] T030 [P] Count a typed command Claude Code expands itself as a start (`S`, `T`). In `normalize`, when `runtime` is `claude`, the record's `role` is `user` and a text block matches `/<command-name>\\s*(\\/[^<\\s]+)\\s*<\\/command-name>/`, add an event of kind `expanded` with `command` set to the captured name. Add `function hostExpanded(events, wanted)`, true when an `expanded` event `namesCommand` the wanted command, and in `startState` add it to the `started` test beside `readDocument` and `reportedStart`. Do not add it to `spokenCommands`. Add a comment saying Claude Code expands a typed command before the model sees it and keeps only this tag in the stored user turn, so the tag is the start. In `T`, add cases on records `[{ id: 'u1', role: 'user', content: [{ type: 'text', text: '<command-message>deep:research</command-message>\\n<command-name>/deep:research</command-name>' }] }]`: `normalize(records, 'claude')` gives one `expanded` event for `/deep:research`, `startState` with expected `/deep:research` and policy `start` gives `started` true, the same with `/deep:review` gives false and `normalize(records, 'pi')` gives no event. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, `node $S --summary $G2 --json | jq -r '.claude.g2.startRate'` prints `3 of 6`, and `node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post.startRate)'` and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.pre.startRate)'` print exactly the same lines as `jq -cS 'map_values(.post.startRate)' $SP/summary-post-before.json` and `jq -cS 'map_values(.pre.startRate)' $SP/summary-pre-before.json`.\n123: - [ ] T031 [P] Say what the capture's `offered` flag means (`CAP`). Above `const offered = landed.some(...)`, add a comment saying the flag is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, a reach measure, and not whether a brief head offered the command, which the behaviour run line records as `offeredCommand`. Change no code. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0 and `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n124: \n125: ### Wave 7\n126: - [ ] T032 Describe every new key and flag in the routing-accuracy README (`RA`). In the scorer row, replace `offerUnknown` with `offerFieldAbsent` and add `cappedOfferRows`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, the loop-without-init rule inside `unsafe` and the Claude `<command-name>` start. In the runner row, add `--brief-only`, the `codex-hooks-unapproved` refusal and the restore to HEAD with `leftoverPaths`. In `### Backfill a finished log`, add that `--brief-only` keeps every offer field and recomputes `briefDelivered`, which Pi, Devin, DSH and Codex now answer and OpenCode does not. Add one sentence where the capture is described: its row `offered` flag means a command bridge is among the top three. Verify: `rg -c \"offerUnknown\" $RA` prints nothing and `rg -o \"offerFieldAbsent|cappedOfferRows|offerReached|deliveryUnknown|offerSeen|brief-only|codex-hooks-unapproved|leftoverPaths|top three|command-name\" $RA | sort -u | wc -l` prints 10.\n127: \n128: ### Wave 7b\n129: - [ ] T039 [P] Keep the command fields in the OpenCode plugin's recommendation mapper (`PLG`, `PLT`). `PLG` is the file to edit: `.opencode/SYNC.md` lists the plugins as authored in place, `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` derives no link for them and the hook-tree entry is a link to `PLG`, so no mirror is regenerated. Run `npm run build` in `ADV` first, because the plugin renders through the built renderer and only phase 012's renderer reads `needsMode`. Add the test first. In `PLT`, right after the `  });` that closes `it('pushes advisor brief into the OpenCode system transform output', ...)`, add this case:\n130:   ```ts\n131:     it.each([\n132:       {\n133:         name: 'a skill row keeps the command and policy the advisor attached',\n134:         recommendation: { skillId: 'sk-doc', kind: 'skill', command: '/create:readme', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12 },\n135:         expectedHead: 'Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.',\n136:       },\n137:       {\n138:         name: 'a hub row keeps the flag that says it needs a mode',\n139:         recommendation: { skillId: 'system-deep-loop', confidence: 0.82, uncertainty: 0.2, needsMode: true },\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 140]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md, lines 120-139\n120: ### Wave 6\n121: - [ ] T029 Refuse an unapproved Codex arm before any turn (`R`). Import `codexHookApproval` from `./command-offer.mjs`. In `main`, after `options.arm` is set and before `runArm`, when `options.runtime` is `codex` and `codexHookApproval({ projectDir: PROJECT_DIR })` returns `'unapproved'`, write `{ ok: false, code: 'codex-hooks-unapproved', runtime: 'codex', measurable: false, repair: 'open /hooks in a Codex session at <PROJECT_DIR> and approve each entry' }` and return `EXIT_REFUSED`. This runs for a dry run too, and nothing writes the approval. Add a comment saying a Codex arm without approval produces zeros that read like refusals, so it is not measurable. Verify: `CODEX_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" node $R --runtime codex --row-id cmd-create-benchmark-plain-tune-01 --out $SP/codex-preflight.jsonl --dry-run; echo exit=$?` prints a line containing `\"code\":\"codex-hooks-unapproved\"` and `exit=2`, and `test -e $SP/codex-preflight.jsonl; echo $?` prints 1. Remove the temporary `CODEX_HOME` folder afterwards.\n122: - [ ] T030 [P] Count a typed command Claude Code expands itself as a start (`S`, `T`). In `normalize`, when `runtime` is `claude`, the record's `role` is `user` and a text block matches `/<command-name>\\s*(\\/[^<\\s]+)\\s*<\\/command-name>/`, add an event of kind `expanded` with `command` set to the captured name. Add `function hostExpanded(events, wanted)`, true when an `expanded` event `namesCommand` the wanted command, and in `startState` add it to the `started` test beside `readDocument` and `reportedStart`. Do not add it to `spokenCommands`. Add a comment saying Claude Code expands a typed command before the model sees it and keeps only this tag in the stored user turn, so the tag is the start. In `T`, add cases on records `[{ id: 'u1', role: 'user', content: [{ type: 'text', text: '<command-message>deep:research</command-message>\\n<command-name>/deep:research</command-name>' }] }]`: `normalize(records, 'claude')` gives one `expanded` event for `/deep:research`, `startState` with expected `/deep:research` and policy `start` gives `started` true, the same with `/deep:review` gives false and `normalize(records, 'pi')` gives no event. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, `node $S --summary $G2 --json | jq -r '.claude.g2.startRate'` prints `3 of 6`, and `node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post.startRate)'` and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.pre.startRate)'` print exactly the same lines as `jq -cS 'map_values(.post.startRate)' $SP/summary-post-before.json` and `jq -cS 'map_values(.pre.startRate)' $SP/summary-pre-before.json`.\n123: - [ ] T031 [P] Say what the capture's `offered` flag means (`CAP`). Above `const offered = landed.some(...)`, add a comment saying the flag is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, a reach measure, and not whether a brief head offered the command, which the behaviour run line records as `offeredCommand`. Change no code. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0 and `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n124: \n125: ### Wave 7\n126: - [ ] T032 Describe every new key and flag in the routing-accuracy README (`RA`). In the scorer row, replace `offerUnknown` with `offerFieldAbsent` and add `cappedOfferRows`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, the loop-without-init rule inside `unsafe` and the Claude `<command-name>` start. In the runner row, add `--brief-only`, the `codex-hooks-unapproved` refusal and the restore to HEAD with `leftoverPaths`. In `### Backfill a finished log`, add that `--brief-only` keeps every offer field and recomputes `briefDelivered`, which Pi, Devin, DSH and Codex now answer and OpenCode does not. Add one sentence where the capture is described: its row `offered` flag means a command bridge is among the top three. Verify: `rg -c \"offerUnknown\" $RA` prints nothing and `rg -o \"offerFieldAbsent|cappedOfferRows|offerReached|deliveryUnknown|offerSeen|brief-only|codex-hooks-unapproved|leftoverPaths|top three|command-name\" $RA | sort -u | wc -l` prints 10.\n127: \n128: ### Wave 7b\n129: - [ ] T039 [P] Keep the command fields in the OpenCode plugin's recommendation mapper (`PLG`, `PLT`). `PLG` is the file to edit: `.opencode/SYNC.md` lists the plugins as authored in place, `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` derives no link for them and the hook-tree entry is a link to `PLG`, so no mirror is regenerated. Run `npm run build` in `ADV` first, because the plugin renders through the built renderer and only phase 012's renderer reads `needsMode`. Add the test first. In `PLT`, right after the `  });` that closes `it('pushes advisor brief into the OpenCode system transform output', ...)`, add this case:\n130:   ```ts\n131:     it.each([\n132:       {\n133:         name: 'a skill row keeps the command and policy the advisor attached',\n134:         recommendation: { skillId: 'sk-doc', kind: 'skill', command: '/create:readme', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12 },\n135:         expectedHead: 'Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.',\n136:       },\n137:       {\n138:         name: 'a hub row keeps the flag that says it needs a mode',\n139:         recommendation: { skillId: 'system-deep-loop', confidence: 0.82, uncertainty: 0.2, needsMode: true },\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 140]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md\",\"offset\":120,\"limit\":20}"},"time":{"start":1794547496577,"end":1794547497306}}}}
