{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794547599629,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","part":{"id":"prt_1d35f490d001PubntNqiqUeSIy","sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","messageID":"msg_1d35f3738001OczBlOtRFPuuJj","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a6f4ea17ba4ea2169a25e506557fc6a13e110e12"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794547602978,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d35f5257002HANFgV4KkxnWYv","sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","messageID":"msg_1d35f3738001OczBlOtRFPuuJj","type":"tool","id":"call_b749da42b1ef435ebe8acffc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch | head -20 && rg -n \"codex-preflight\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md"},"output":"before.txt\nbriefs\ndelivery-before.txt\nlogs\nplanning\nsummary-g2-before.json\nsummary-post-before.json\nsummary-pre-before.json\n121:- [ ] T029 Refuse an unapproved Codex arm before any turn (`R`). Import `codexHookApproval` from `./command-offer.mjs`. In `main`, after `options.arm` is set and before `runArm`, when `options.runtime` is `codex` and `codexHookApproval({ projectDir: PROJECT_DIR })` returns `'unapproved'`, write `{ ok: false, code: 'codex-hooks-unapproved', runtime: 'codex', measurable: false, repair: 'open /hooks in a Codex session at <PROJECT_DIR> and approve each entry' }` and return `EXIT_REFUSED`. This runs for a dry run too, and nothing writes the approval. Add a comment saying a Codex arm without approval produces zeros that read like refusals, so it is not measurable. Verify: `CODEX_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" node $R --runtime codex --row-id cmd-create-benchmark-plain-tune-01 --out $SP/codex-preflight.jsonl --dry-run; echo exit=$?` prints a line containing `\"code\":\"codex-hooks-unapproved\"` and `exit=2`, and `test -e $SP/codex-preflight.jsonl; echo $?` prints 1. Remove the temporary `CODEX_HOME` folder afterwards.\n176:- [ ] T037 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create`