{"type":"text","timestamp":1794547616546,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","part":{"id":"prt_1d35f8b17002hMJcIMFoTHN9Al","sessionID":"ses_e2ca2ab7affegsDeF1ZxNlGowy","messageID":"msg_1d35f70050017P4B4PSW2d1G3m","type":"text","text":"Task complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`\n  - Imported `codexHookApproval` from `./command-offer.mjs`.\n  - In `main`, after `options.arm` is set and before `runArm`, added the Codex preflight: when `options.runtime === 'codex'` and `codexHookApproval({ projectDir: PROJECT_DIR })` returns `'unapproved'`, it writes `{ ok: false, code: 'codex-hooks-unapproved', runtime: 'codex', measurable: false, repair: ... }` and returns `EXIT_REFUSED` (2). It is not gated on `--dry-run`, and it writes no approval. The comment states the durability reason: zeros from an unapproved arm read like refusals, so the arm is not measurable.\n\nThe rest of the diff on that file is earlier-wave work already present in the tree (restore module, `--brief-only`, shared reader); I did not touch or revert it.\n\n## Verify output\n\nCommand (with `$SP` and `$R` substituted, temp `CODEX_HOME` removed afterwards):\n\n```\nCODEX_HOME=\"$TMP_CODEX_HOME\" node \"$R\" --runtime codex \\\n  --row-id cmd-create-benchmark-plain-tune-01 \\\n  --out \"$SP/codex-preflight.jsonl\" --dry-run; echo \"exit=$?\"\ntest -e \"$SP/codex-preflight.jsonl\"; echo \"exists=$?\"\n```\n\nPrinted:\n\n```\n{\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"codex-hooks-unapproved\",\"runtime\":\"codex\",\"measurable\":false,\"repair\":\"open /hooks in a Codex session at /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research and approve each entry\"}\nexit=2\nexists=1\nremoved /var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/tmp.ETCorRCtvN\n```\n\n- Contains `\"code\":\"codex-hooks-unapproved\"` — yes.\n- `exit=2` — yes.\n- `test -e $SP/codex-preflight.jsonl` prints 1 — yes (absent).\n- Temporary `CODEX_HOME` folder removed — yes.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The task line does not name `plan.md`, so I did not read it.\n- Nothing in `tasks.md` was ticked; T029 remains `- [ ]`.\n- No git state changed. The only untracked entry added by the verify would have been the preflight log, and it was correctly not written.","time":{"start":1794547616536,"end":1794547616546}}}
